# 1. Proteomics


@top-left


![Student-created workflow from sample collection to protein identification.](assets/lect04c-talking_points_set_3/student_proteomics-workflow.jpg)


@bottom-left


![Instructor figure related to protein abundance](assets/lect04c-talking_points_set_3/image_001.png)


@right


- Protein abundance
- Protein identity
- Biological state
=== layout: one-plus-two-panels


# Questions: Proteomics


@left


- How does a proteome differ from a genome, and why does it change across cells and conditions?
- How do researchers separate, identify, and quantify proteins in a complex sample?
- What can proteomics reveal about disease, cell function, or biotechnology products?


@top-right


![Instructor figure related to protein abundance](assets/lect04c-talking_points_set_3/image_002.jpg)


@bottom-right


![Student-created workflow from sample collection to protein identification.](assets/lect04c-talking_points_set_3/student_proteomics-workflow.jpg)
=== layout: one-plus-two-panels


# Answers: Proteomics


@left


- A genome records DNA; a proteome is the set of proteins present in a cell or sample at a given time.
- Protein abundance, isoforms, interactions, activity, and post-translational modifications all vary.
- A common workflow extracts proteins, digests them into peptides, separates them, and analyzes them by mass spectrometry.


@top-right


![Student-created workflow from sample collection to protein identification.](assets/lect04c-talking_points_set_3/student_proteomics-workflow.jpg)


@bottom-right


![Instructor figure related to protein abundance](assets/lect04c-talking_points_set_3/image_001.png)
=== layout: one-plus-two-panels


# Answers: Proteomics - Interpreting the data


@left


- Spectra are matched to protein databases; statistical controls help limit false identifications.
- Proteomics can find candidate biomarkers, drug targets, pathway changes, or product-quality differences.
- Results depend on the tissue, condition, sampling time, and measurement method; one sample is not a complete proteome.


@top-right


![Instructor figure related to protein abundance](assets/lect04c-talking_points_set_3/image_001.png)


@bottom-right


![Instructor figure related to protein abundance](assets/lect04c-talking_points_set_3/image_002.jpg)
=== layout: two-panels


# Answers: Proteomics - From sample to proteome


@left


- Collect matched biological replicates and record tissue, condition, treatment, and collection time.
- Extract proteins, digest them into peptides, separate by liquid chromatography, then analyze peptides by tandem mass spectrometry.
- Search peptide spectra against a sequence database and apply statistical thresholds to control false identifications.


@right


![Student-created workflow from sample collection to protein identification.](assets/lect04c-talking_points_set_3/student_proteomics-workflow.jpg)
=== layout: one-plus-two-panels


